  "description": "T1: Rowan (dead): Fell. T2: Lawson Cypress: Crown lift removing 1 x branch above footpath + 5 x branches above border. Remove deadwood target prune stubs. T3: Norway Spruce:  Crown lift removing 1 x branch above footpath + 3 x branches above border. Remove deadwood. T4: Purple Leaf Plum: Crown reduce top of crown by up to 3m to re-shape giving clearance to adjacent property. G2: Silver Birch x 3: Crown reduce over-extended lateral branches to reshape. Crown thin 15% removing any deadwood. Prune to give clearance to adjacent trees. T5: Sweet Chestnut: NO WORKS.  T6: Robinia  (Acacia):  Create pollard at approx. 6m retaining suckering live growth. T7: Crab Apple:  Remove major deadwood. T8: Magnolia:  NO WORKS.  T9: Sycamore (twin-stemmed( dead):  Fell. T10: Sycamore (multi-stemmed) - Fell. T11: Philadelphus - Fell. G3: Laurel: Fell 2 x smaller stems adjacent to corner of property to a point as close to ground level as is reasonably practicable. Prune back remaining lateral branches to 2m from edge of footpath.  G4: Bamboo:  Fell.  Rambling  Rose:  Prune back to 1m from edge of footpath. Laurel:  Trim all round giving clearance to adjacent property. T12: Purple Leaf Plum: Crown reduce top of crown by up to 3m to previous pruning points. Reduce lateral branches to re-shape giving clearance to adjacent property of crown by up to 3m to previous pruning points. Reduce lateral branches to re-shape giving clearance to adjacent property.",
